    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0212" n="1262" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/6–2552: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Pakistan</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d713-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-06-26T16:28:00-04:00">June 26, 1952—4:28
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1396. Re Kashmir. Emb’s niact tel 1563.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d713-f2"/></p>
                <p>In view: (a) indicated intention of Pak Del in NY to stop negots with Graham on
                    June 26 or shortly thereafter; (b) info contained in reftel indicating poss
                    willingness Nazimuddin to consider different figure on troop quantum; (c) our
                    understanding Graham desires Ayub stay in NY, you are requested urge Nazimuddin
                    or Zafrulla as you see fit to direct Ayub to remain in NY for poss further
                    negots along lines Nazimuddin has indicated GOP might be prepared to consider.
                    You may indicates US greatly interested in Nazimuddin’s consideration of new
                    figure for troop quantum.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d713-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d713-f1-content">
